BossLog: {
	Megashark.SpawnInfo: Once the three machines have fallen, twenty rounds from a Minishark into the sea. It comes up under you.
	Abomanation.SpawnInfo: Let small things run free on the Wasted Mile. Bunnies, squirrels, red squirrels. No rodent will get away, and the tenth brings them.
	GildedKnight.SpawnInfo: Climb to the willows under the great white wall. He keeps the road before it. After, ring the spur he leaves on that same field.
}

Hints: {
	ClothierMile: Landwards, opposite the sea, there is a mile where nothing calls. I would not let a bunny go there. One goes quiet. Ten will go quiet. Then something answers. Hee hee. Not that I have been, yknow?
	Offering: These may satiate one and many.
	GuideLegends: I feel like the balance of the world is disturbed, I can feel the intangible ominous presence everywhere. Did you do something?
	GuideArsenal: An incantation does nothing sitting in your pack. You have to learn it by heart first, and I've only ever seen that done near a house with residential life. Then you say it through a seal. Spells want a staff instead.
	GuideAltar: Incantations were written, not taught. A book and an altar and you could knock together from bones and wood, and something foul to write with. Nobody I've asked knows what.
	GuideKingdom: Far {0}, past the field where every tree is a stump, there's a wall taller than any tree ever grew. A kingdom's, my books say. Its gates are still shut. The books don't say who shut them.
	GuidePilgrim: A man came through here leaning on a bow taller than he was, with a huge sword on his back too. He told me his name twice and laugh loudly, as if the first time might not have taken.
	GuideHut: I scouted the area before your awakening. On the trail seawards, there is a little hut, tethered yet foreboding. I'm too much of a coward and dared not enter. Do me a favour and tell me what is inside.
	DryadBezoar: There is a wound in my side that has not closed in years. Leaves do nothing for it. A Bezoar would draw it out. The hornets carry them, though not often.
	DryadRoots: Since the wound closed I can hear the roots again. Most of them rest. Some have not stopped in years, and things with mouths grow up out of them. Cut six of those roots and bring them to me. I want to know how far down it goes.
	DryadRootsThanks: Still growing, even cut. Something used to stop them, and I never had to think about it. Take this. It is how a root goes when it is sent, and it will not stop for you either.
}

Subworlds: {
	DoorNotAlone: It does not open while others share the world.
	DoorForgot: It has forgotten where it leads.
	DoorWall: It opened onto a wall.

